Tell the bundled skill how an ask reaches an attached session from an ngterm-headless origin. The headless origin
draws nothing, so it hands an `ask open` to the presenting machine whatever the presenter roles. A program in an
attached session gives `--target "$NGTERM_SESSION_ID"` to `ask`: without a target, a terminal ask goes to the
session that the origin has selected, and a GUI ask stays in the origin's window. Applied after
0025-attach-all-first.patch.

